Z||000007||2birds||09-17-2001||01:10 AM||||8ball, your switch is probably grounded from water, or just worn out.  When I lived in the Puget Sound area, my front trunk switch was wet from all the rain (year-round).  It's not very well protected||||reg||1
Z||000008||johnt671||09-17-2001||07:01 PM||||Had the same problem when I first got mine.  Dash looked pretty between the check engine, seat belt and ajar lights flashing. Those were the days.  I took a close look at mine and just bent the mounting bracket up a hair.<p>[This message has been edited by johnt671 (edited 09-17-2001).]||||reg||1
